{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Science or Science Fiction?", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Everyday Objects ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Real Conditional: Talking About The Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the Real <span class=\"italic\">Conditional</span> with If clauses to talk about future situations and outcomes.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If you're going to move into the future with your home appliances, soon you'll have a lot of ultramodern gadgets to choose from. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You use the Real Conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not, will, or will not happen. <br> The parts of the sentence are divided into two clauses: the <span class=\"italic\"> If</span> clause and  the <span class=\"italic\">Condition </span>clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">If + Present Simple/Present continuous \u2026 will/Present Continuous / be going to</span>  <br>Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> We'll need a holographic TV if we're going to keep up.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use an Imperative verb in the main clause if you are making offers, giving instructions, or suggesting advice.   <br>Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> Get one of these if you want to save water.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you wait for that new stove, you'll be able to change the way you cook altogether soon with heatless cooking. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you are wondering what it is, you'll be finding out right here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you use an induction cooktop, just the pot you are using and what's inside will heat up. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Choose an induction stove if you want the heat to be generated on the pan rather than from the stovetop.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Verbs Followed by -ing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk about two actions linked together, you normally use two verbs. The first verb follows the rules of conjugation for the sentence, while the second verb can be a verb in the -ing form.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I don't mind waiting for new innovations, do you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You can use two verbs to talk about two connected actions. The main verb introduces the main action, and the second verb in the -ing form gives more information about that action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some verbs followed by -ing are <span class=\"italic\">imagine, enjoy, consider, mind, keep, love/hate </span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Subject + first verb + -ing form of the second verb</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at some examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Stores in the U.S. are anticipating getting this technology soon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Consider cooking on a stove with electromagnetic currents in the burners that make the metal pots and pans hot. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Imagine taking a pan off the stovetop and then being able to put your hand on the cool glass surface.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A new company is proposing finding ways to refresh holographic images faster. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "With this you will enjoy seeing things move and look  as they should. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Keep looking for them at a store near you!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ultramodern ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "most recently developed and put on the market", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you're going to move into the future with your home appliances, soon you'll have a lot of ultramodern gadgets to choose from.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about appliances of the future.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "innovation ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a new idea or method", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I don't mind waiting for new innovations, do you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to anticipate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to imagine or expect something to happen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Stores in the U.S. are anticipating getting this technology soon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "heatless ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without generating heat", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you wait for that new stove, you'll be able to change the way you cook altogether soon with heatless cooking. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "electromagnetic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the interrelation of electricity and a magnetic field", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Consider cooking on a stove with electromagnetic currents in the burners that make the metal pots and pans hot.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "induction ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "heating and object without electricity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you use an induction cooktop, just the pot you are cooking with and what's inside it gets hot.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "burner ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "part of stove which produces heat for cooking", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Imagine removing a pan from  the burner it's no longer hot.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "holographic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "projecting 3D images created by light beams", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If we're going to have holographic TVs for the consumer market, the new, quick refresh rates will have to work and keep working. Keep looking for them at a store near you!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "waterless ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without the use of water", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are also recommending waiting for the hero of the century, the waterless washing machine.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "absorbent ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "able to take in liquids", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:These beads are more absorbent than water, allowing them to absorb stains right into their core.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob01aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Decide on a new appliance that people will want to use.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sketch out a basic drawing or use a picture that's of something similar and annotate it with the innovations and how they are used.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about using this item in the future with \"if\".", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your appliance to a partner or group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to other presentations", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss the advantages of such items together.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I decide on a new appliance that people will want to use.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I annotate an image of the item.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about the item using real conditionals and verbs followed by gerunds.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss items with a partner or group.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instruc